WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.160
Remediation begins by updating controlled source inputs: the base image reference,

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:10.660
operating-system packages, language runtime, lock files, application libraries, or code.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.400
Build from a reviewed definition rather than altering a running container,

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:17.740
then assign the result a new immutable image digest.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:22.440
Automated tests should confirm that the image starts, passes health checks,

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:24.900
and preserves application behavior.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.840
Unit and security tests catch local failures.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:34.700
Integration tests verify databases, messaging, identity, storage, and external services.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:39.640
A representative staging environment reveals deployment and platform interactions.

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:42.500
Review changes beyond the named vulnerability.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:47.840
A newer base may update certificates, libraries, defaults, system users,

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:49.660
or architecture support.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:53.320
Dependency upgrades may change APIs or data formats.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:57.380
Patch testing should reflect the application's actual operating paths.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:01.760
Roll out through a controlled strategy such as rolling replacement, canary exposure,

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:04.060
or blue-green deployment when appropriate.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:08.040
Monitor errors, latency, resource use, health,

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:10.900
and business indicators while the new image is introduced.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:14.880
Pause or reverse the rollout when defined limits are exceeded.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:20.380
Rollback planning identifies a known-good image and the conditions for returning to it.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:24.600
It must also account for database migrations, message schemas,

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:29.220
or external changes that may not be reversible merely by selecting an older container.

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:35.520
Immutable infrastructure makes the deployed state traceable: rebuild, test, sign, promote,

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:37.740
deploy, and verify.

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:42.520
Emergency patches may compress timelines, but they should not abandon provenance,

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:47.460
essential tests, monitoring, or follow-up work that restores the standard process.
